# How can you possibly measure how bad an illness feels? A map of the methods
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical","b":"gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical"}
next: {"title":"Time trade-off and standard gamble: whose values, and what lies below zero?","href":"https://drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/dcast/health-technology-assessment-deciding/time-trade-off-and-standard-gamble-whose.cast"}

## The Missing Number
voice: male
level: basic
domain: {"x":[0,12],"y":[0,1]}

    axes ax x_label "Years of life" y_label "Health utility u" hidden true
    curve full_health dashed #8f887c expr "1" hidden true
    label label_full "u = 1: full health" below #8f887c attach_to full_health hidden true
    curve untreated #b5482e expr "0.28 - 0.06*x" x_from 0 x_to 2 hidden true
    label label_untreated "Untreated SMA type 1" above-left #b5482e attach_to untreated hidden true
    dot death_pt #b5482e at.x 2 at.y 0.16 hidden true
    label label_death "Death before age two" right #b5482e attach_to death_pt hidden true
    curve treated dashed #2f6b8f expr "0.55" x_from 0 x_to 11 hidden true
    label label_treated "Treated with nusinersen" above #2f6b8f attach_to treated hidden true
    curve baseline #8f887c expr "0" x_from 0 x_to 11 style.opacity 0.15 hidden true
    region qaly_area x_from 0 x_to 11 between ["treated","baseline"] style.fill #f2c14e style.opacity 0.3 hidden true
    label label_area "QALYs = u × time" below attach_to qaly_area hidden true
    arrow time_arrow from.x 2 from.y 0.08 to.x 11 to.y 0.08 hidden true
    label label_time "≈ 9 extra years" below attach_to time_arrow hidden true
    arrow u_arrow #8a5fa8 from.x 6 from.y 0 to.x 6 to.y 0.55 hidden true
    label label_u "u = ?" right #8a5fa8 attach_to u_arrow hidden true
    mark mark_u target label_u kind box hidden true
    box state_node "u for one health state" hidden true
    box n_direct "Direct valuation" hidden true
    box n_indirect "Indirect instruments" hidden true
    box n_dce "Discrete choice experiments" hidden true
    edge e_direct state_node -> n_direct hidden true
    edge e_indirect state_node -> n_indirect hidden true
    edge e_dce state_node -> n_dce hidden true
    label lab_direct "VAS, time trade-off, standard gamble" below attach_to n_direct hidden true
    label lab_indirect "EQ-5D, SF-6D, 15D — plus a value set" below attach_to n_indirect hidden true
    label lab_dce "Choices between states, not ratings" below attach_to n_dce hidden true

Across these five parts we map every method health economists use to put a number on how bad an illness feels — and this figure is why they need one.
    draw ax full_health label_full

Our running case: spinal muscular atrophy type one, where an infant's motor neurons fail within months, and untreated, most children die or depend on a ventilator before their second birthday.
    draw untreated label_untreated death_pt label_death

    pause 0.3

Nusinersen changes that picture — treated children survive for years, many of them still ventilated.
    draw treated label_treated

    pause 0.3

The trial hands us the width of that survival: call it roughly nine extra years of life.
    draw time_arrow label_time

But no health system buys years; it buys quality-adjusted years — and a QALY is an area, utility multiplied by time.
    draw baseline qaly_area label_area

    pause 0.4

So everything rests on the height of this box: what is u for the state 'SMA type one, ventilated, treated'?
    draw u_arrow label_u

And here is the awkward fact — no scanner, no blood test, no motor-function score ever outputs zero point four.
    camera center.ref label_u zoom 2.2

u is not a property of the body at all; it is a statement about how much people would give up to escape that state.
    camera reset true

    pause 0.5

Which means the number has to come from human judgement — and there are three families of ways to get it.
    clear

Start from the state we need valued.
    draw state_node

The first family values it directly: describe the state to people, then ask them to place it on a scale, or trade years of life away, or gamble against death.
    draw e_direct n_direct lab_direct

The second never asks the patient to value anything — they simply describe their own health in a handful of questions, and a ready-made value set converts that description into a number.
    draw e_indirect n_indirect lab_indirect

That split, where one person describes the state and a quite different sample of people values it, is the spine of everything ahead.
    highlight n_indirect effect glow

The third asks for no number at all: just repeated choices between two health states, with the values reconstructed from the pattern of choosing.
    draw e_dce n_dce lab_dce

EQ-5D-5L alone describes three thousand one hundred and twenty-five states, and each carries a value that differs by country — Norway now has a value set of its own.
    point at.ref n_indirect gesture tap

    pause 0.4

Which family you pick is not a technicality.
    clear

Move this height by five hundredths and nusinersen's ICER moves by millions of kroner — and the very same missing height sits under hip replacements and statins, where small differences multiply across hundreds of thousands of patients.
    show ax full_health untreated label_untreated death_pt label_death treated label_treated baseline qaly_area label_area time_arrow label_time u_arrow label_u

So the question for the rest of this series is exactly this one box.
    draw mark_u delivery grave

Every method ahead — scales, trade-offs, gambles, questionnaires, choice tasks — exists to fill in a number that no machine can read.

## The Tariff Is a Separate Artefact
voice: male
level: basic
sources:
    - id: dolan1997
      title: Modeling valuations for EuroQol health states
      authors: Dolan
      year: 1997
      finding: UK EQ-5D-3L tariff; state 33333 = −0.594
    - id: shaw2005
      title: 'US valuation of the EQ-5D health states: development and testing of the D1 valuation model'
      authors: Shaw, Johnson and Coons
      year: 2005
      finding: US EQ-5D-3L tariff; state 33333 = −0.109

    text head "EQ-5D-5L: the descriptive system" x 500 y 700 font_size 32 hidden true
    text d_mob "Mobility" x 250 y 620 font_size 26 hidden true
    text d_self "Self-care" x 250 y 565 font_size 26 hidden true
    text d_act "Usual activities" x 250 y 510 font_size 26 hidden true
    text d_pain "Pain / discomfort" x 250 y 455 font_size 26 hidden true
    text d_anx "Anxiety / depression" x 250 y 400 font_size 26 hidden true
    text l_mob "5 — unable to walk about" #2f6b8f x 660 y 620 font_size 24 hidden true
    text l_self "5 — unable to wash or dress" #2f6b8f x 660 y 565 font_size 24 hidden true
    text l_act "5 — unable to do usual activities" #2f6b8f x 660 y 510 font_size 24 hidden true
    text l_pain "5 — extreme pain" #2f6b8f x 660 y 455 font_size 24 hidden true
    text l_anx "4 — severely anxious" #2f6b8f x 660 y 400 font_size 24 hidden true
    text code "State  5 5 5 5 4" #b5482e x 500 y 290 font_size 48 hidden true
    text count "5 levels × 5 dimensions = 3 125 possible states — and no values" #8f887c x 500 y 200 font_size 24 hidden true
    box n_public "Public sample (n ≈ 1 000)" hidden true
    box n_task "TTO / DCE valuation tasks" hidden true
    box n_model "Regression model" hidden true
    box n_tariff "Value set: 3 125 states → u" hidden true
    arrow a1 n_public -> n_task hidden true
    arrow a2 n_task -> n_model hidden true
    arrow a3 n_model -> n_tariff hidden true

Follow the indirect route to u all the way down — because a submission can lose its utility number to a decision made in another country, years before the patient was ill.
    draw head d_mob d_self d_act d_pain d_anx

A child with spinal muscular atrophy: her proxy ticks unable to walk about, unable to wash or dress, unable to do her usual activities, extreme pain, severely anxious.
    draw l_mob l_self l_act l_pain l_anx parallel true

And that is the entire output of the descriptive system — the state five, five, five, five, four.
    draw code

An address, not a price.
    point at.ref code gesture circle

One of three thousand one hundred and twenty-five addresses, and the questionnaire values none of them.
    draw count

The value comes from somewhere else entirely — a separate study, run years earlier, on completely different people.
    clear

A national sample of the general public: about a thousand ordinary citizens, most of them in decent health.
    draw n_public

They value a handful of states by trading off time, or by choosing between them — last part's direct methods, now applied to strangers' hypothetical lives.
    draw a1 n_task

A regression fits a coefficient to every level of every dimension, and out drops the tariff — a lookup table pricing all 3 125 states, including the thousands nobody ever valued.
    draw a2 n_model a3 n_tariff

Two separate artefacts: the patient says which state she is in, the public says what that state is worth.
    label t_who "Patients describe. The public values." below attach_to n_tariff

So when the tariff changes, the number changes — although nothing about the patient has.
    clear

    text st3 "EQ-5D-3L, worst state  3 3 3 3 3" x 500 y 620 font_size 30
    path nl_line points [[140,380],[900,380]]
    path zero_tick points [[453,365],[453,395]]
    path one_tick points [[900,365],[900,395]]
    text lab_zero "0 = dead" x 453 y 425 font_size 22
    text lab_one "1 = full health" x 850 y 425 font_size 22
    text lab_worse "worse than dead" #8f887c x 250 y 425 font_size 22

Take the older three-level EQ-5D at its worst state, three-three-three-three-three. The British value set puts it at minus 0.594 — well below being dead.
    path uk_tick thick #2f6b8f points [[187,355],[187,405]]
    text uk_label "UK:  −0.594" #2f6b8f cites ["dolan1997"] x 187 y 320 font_size 26

The American value set, same questionnaire, same five ticks, says minus 0.109.
    path us_tick thick #b5482e points [[404,355],[404,405]]
    text us_label "US:  −0.109" #b5482e cites ["shaw2005"] x 404 y 320 font_size 26
    delivery grave

Almost half a unit of utility sits between those two marks, every year, for every patient in that state.
    camera center.x 300 center.y 310 zoom 2

The gap is purely the tariff: different samples, different elicitation protocols, different statistical models of the very same description.
    arrow gap_arrow #8a5fa8 from.x 187 from.y 270 to.x 404 to.y 270
    text gap_label "0.485 utility — from the tariff alone" #8a5fa8 x 300 y 230 font_size 26
    mark mark target gap_label kind box

    camera reset true

Norwegian submissions long borrowed the British tariff, for want of a Norwegian one — so the utilities reaching Beslutningsforum carried English preferences about disability.
    text note_norway "Norwegian submissions long used the UK tariff" #8f887c x 500 y 150 font_size 24

And since the QALY gain is the utility change times time, swapping value sets rescales ΔE, and with it nusinersen's ICER, without one clinical fact changing.
    text note_icer "ΔE = Δu × time    →    ICER = ΔC / ΔE" x 500 y 85 font_size 26

The descriptive system measures her illness; the value set is a national artefact — and it is the second one that decides what her illness is worth.
    focus note_icer note_norway

